      7: P2+
    for a quadrilateral
      8: Q2
    for a hexahedron
      8: Q2
    for a tetrahedron
      6: P2 
    for a prism
     16: P2Q2
    NOTE: for high-order or spectral, also the polynomial order p needs to be
          set with coefficients%i(51). See examples.

2   pressure interpolation (base function). Low order choices:
    for a triangle
      2: P1
    for a quadrilateral
      2: P1
      4: Q1 
