67  Use a 3D velocity vector in a 2D space:
      0: no 
      1: yes
    NOTE: the definition of the third velocity component depends on the
          coordinate system used (coefficients%i(23)):
     * velocity component u_z in the 2D Cartesian system (coefficients%i(23)=0).
     * circumferential velocity component u_theta in the axisymmetrical case,
       i.e. add "swirl". (coefficients%i(23)=1).
    NOTE: Not all elements have been modified to take this into account.
          An error message is given if incompatible elements are called.  
    NOTE: Not all add-ons have implemented the third component. Hence, check
          the elements before using coefficients%i(67)=1.

